      "facts": "Pokemon_IsGroundForbidden queries first, then either the nine-value integer default switch or an exact-float custom replacement ending at zero/first match. Pokemon_StepWalk queries next X/Z directly into currGround; if permitted, probes old AUX plus normalized velocity times signed collisionRadius using a separate ground temporary; exact fixed-height test precedes X/Z and optional ground-Y publication. No source targetPos, pos1, euler, root-local animation, yaw, tangibility or collPosition mutation occurs in this leaf."
    },
    "src/app_level/app_level.h": {
      "git_blob": "953e57fd6e9d76a3962068fb5aefa93d9f55b3d4",
      "sha256": "b95ed8883bc54021ff82df89a6846b16c487e781215eb71f241dbaff194f60e4",
      "spans": [
        [
          115,
          124
        ]
      ],
      "facts": "Movement ON_GROUND is bit0x01 and FIXED_HEIGHT bit0x10. The other movement flags do not gain behavior in StepWalk."
    },
    "src/sys/vector.c": {
      "git_blob": "99b21e6c073cdbce135abfc10533defc56a05026",
      "sha256": "f36b6f36e6e1434bd498d41df4b03e63775d8f765dc6337f76a7ccfbb5c9fa57",
      "spans": [
        [
          5,
          16
        ],
        [
          54,
          60
        ]
      ],
      "facts": "Walk normalization uses sqrtf of left-associated binary32 squares and reciprocal multiplication. Zero magnitude returns without modifying the vector, including a nonzero component whose square underflows. Infinite squared magnitude from finite components is defined and gives zero components via reciprocal multiplication. Signed radius scale follows normalization; the different existing world_collision division helper is not reused."
    },
    "src/world/ground.c": {
      "git_blob": "3a224b70ccbb73fca7138d0f5b5da7c17d7a6de2",
      "sha256": "88d9003eee13aadb2d344596cb8b08a461e9ceca0b9d0975d06eced8dee822a9",
      "spans": [
        [
          40,
          86
        ]
      ],
      "facts": "Absent current block, descriptor or height map gives height-9000, up normal and unsigned-minus-one surface. Coordinates transform as query/100 plus current-block world X/Z; block world elevation is subtracted before height times100. Full World normal including source up-axis swap and signed surface converted to native uint32 is retained, not reconstructed from height. The source walk ignores the ground boolean."
    },
    "src/world/ground_int.c": {
      "git_blob": "83c264a3f8a579e25b1bdec0a95a9e61f9ada8d0",
      "sha256": "9a9682b79d156d56102c5f4cc3a6587366d2fac9d28eaa9110b1104b2ba39c9f",
      "spans": [
        [
          72,
          96
        ],
        [
          102,
          112
        ],
        [
          118,
          137
        ]
      ],
      "facts": "Ground branch equality selects right, patch takes precedence over child, and an uncovered branch returns NULL. ground.c then dereferences its missing normal: native ground_query rejects consumed uncovered/malformed paths rather than silently manufacturing fallback ground. Plane C zero gives zero height; no synthetic unit normal or new nonnegative-radius/underflow policy is added. Source unsigned patch surface shifts eight and masks24 bits."
    },
    "src/world/world.h": {
      "git_blob": "0a4069418ecaefcfa6a859f860cd68ca3d4b89d4",
      "sha256": "e3f0ed6c34c041958994e4e4091fbf7f4564afffa14aff24439d21378f4822a3",
      "spans": [
        [
          172,
          193
        ]
      ],
      "facts": "Default forbidden nine surface values are 007F66/00FF00/337FB2/4CCCCC/7F6633/7F667F/FF0000/FF4C19/FF7FB2."
    }
